WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.325
A topology describes how nodes and links are arranged.

00:00:04.325 --> 00:00:09.130
Physical topology concerns actual connections; logical topology concerns communication relationships.

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:18.260
Star, bus, ring and mesh models help compare cost, failure behaviour and manageability, but real deployments may combine them.

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:22.443
A failed PC cable usually disconnects that PC.

00:00:22.443 --> 00:00:26.820
A failed central switch can disconnect every PC relying on it.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:32.390
Redundant design can reduce this dependency, but redundancy must be deliberately planned and tested.

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:37.676
How many links connect four nodes in a full undirected mesh?

00:00:37.676 --> 00:00:39.235
Use n(n−1)/2, giving 6.
